1. Executive Summary
Mundra Brothers operates as an UltraTech Cement non-trade dealer on a commission basis. Mundra Brothers sources and manages clients, while UltraTech Cement invoices those clients directly. Mundra Brothers must therefore control customer POs and dispatch requests, commercial rates, payment terms, credit limits, payment follow-up, ledger reconciliation, balance confirmations, compliance documents and commission-related processes without being the billing entity.
The proposed product will be a white-label web application branded for Mundra Brothers. Each client organization will receive its own secure workspace. Client users will be able to create authorized POs, request full or partial dispatches, report payments, allocate payments against invoices, request ledgers, complete balance confirmations, raise disputes and manage their internal users. Mundra Brothers will manage client terms, pricing, approval rules, exceptions, documents, alerts and all operational controls from a separate administration portal.
Primary product outcome: No non-trade dispatch should proceed without a transparent, auditable decision based on credit exposure, payment-term compliance, balance-confirmation compliance and authorized exceptions.

2. Business Context and Problem Statement
2.1 Current Business Model
•	Mundra Brothers sells UltraTech Cement to its clients on a commission basis.
•	UltraTech Cement raises invoices directly in the name of Mundra Brothers' clients.
•	Client payments, payment realization and applicable commercial terms influence commission and operational eligibility.
•	Mundra Brothers is responsible for controlling client relationships, rates, POs, dispatches, credit exposure, overdue payments, documentation and follow-up.
2.2 Problems to Be Solved
•	Dispatch requests may be received without a consistent real-time check of credit limit, overdue status or compliance documents.
•	Client payment updates may remain pending with Mundra Brothers even after the client has paid, creating avoidable dispatch blocks and disputes.
•	Payment allocation, TDS treatment and refund-letter preparation require manual work and are vulnerable to errors.
•	Quarterly balance confirmations require repeated emailing, document tracking, client signatures, stamps and internal verification.
•	Different people within a client organization need different permissions and approval responsibilities.
•	Mundra Brothers also needs internal role-based access so accounts, PO/dispatch-processing and approvers only see and perform permitted actions.
•	Clients require a clear view of why a PO or dispatch request is approved, held or blocked and a direct mechanism to resolve incorrect ledger or payment information.
•	Follow-ups for outstanding payments, expiring credit availability and pending balance confirmations are currently difficult to automate and audit.
3. Product Vision, Goals and Scope
3.1 Product Vision
Create a trusted digital control centre for Mundra Brothers' non-trade client operations, allowing clients to transact independently while ensuring that every commercially sensitive action follows configurable approval, credit and compliance rules.
3.2 Goals
•	Provide a fully white-labelled Mundra Brothers experience.
•	Enable client self-service for POs, dispatch requests, payment updates, ledgers, issues and balance confirmations.
•	Automate dispatch eligibility checks and route exceptions to authorized Mundra Brothers approvers.
•	Reduce manual preparation of refund letters and balance-confirmation follow-ups.
•	Maintain a single auditable record of POs, dispatches, payments, approvals, documents and communications.
•	Prevent new dispatches when configured credit, overdue or balance-confirmation rules are violated unless a valid special approval exists.
•	Give management real-time visibility into exposure, overdue amounts, blocked dispatches and pending actions.
3.3 Non-Goals for the Initial Release
•	Replacing UltraTech's ERP, invoicing or dispatch systems.
•	Acting as a general accounting platform or replacing Tally unless a future integration is approved.
•	Calculating final dealer commission until the exact UltraTech commission and settlement rules are provided.
•	Managing physical logistics in detail unless allocation, dispatch and vehicle data become part of a later phase.
•	Providing an open public marketplace. Access is limited to approved organizations and users.
