4.2 Permission Principles
•	Permissions must be configurable at organization, module and action level: view, create, edit, submit, approve, reject, download and administer.
•	Client Organization Admins may create multiple users but may only grant permissions allowed to their organization by Mundra Brothers.
•	Maker-checker approval must be configurable separately for POs, dispatch requests, payment submissions and balance confirmations.
•	A user must not approve their own submission when maker-checker is enabled.
•	Sensitive actions such as credit-limit changes, special approvals, rate overrides and permission changes must always be logged.
•	Deactivated users must immediately lose access while their historic actions remain visible in the audit trail.
