6. Functional Requirements
FR-01 | White-Label Branding
The application must appear as a Mundra Brothers-owned digital service.
•	Display Mundra Brothers' logo, product name, approved colour palette, contact details and legal footer.
•	Use branded email templates, PDF templates, login screens and notification content.
•	Keep branding configuration editable by authorized super administrators without a software release.
•	Do not expose the software vendor's branding to ordinary users unless contractually required.
FR-02 | Authentication and Persistent Sessions
Users must have secure but low-friction access.
•	The first screen must request username/email and password.
•	Support secure password reset, account lockout after repeated failures and administrator-led user deactivation.
•	Keep users signed in through a secure persistent session for a configurable duration so they do not need to log in repeatedly.
•	Require re-authentication for sensitive actions or after risk signals such as a password change, unusual device or long inactivity.
•	Allow an administrator to revoke all active sessions for a user or organization.
•	Optional future support: OTP or multi-factor authentication for approvers and administrators.
FR-03 | Client Organization and User Management
Each client must operate in an isolated organization workspace.
•	Create a separate tenant/account for every client organization.
•	Allow the Client Organization Admin to invite, create, deactivate and manage multiple users.
•	Allow role templates as well as custom permission combinations.
•	Allow the client to configure internal maker-checker approval for POs, dispatch requests and payments.
•	Provide a user activity log showing account creation, permission changes, submissions and approvals.
•	During onboarding, allow an authorized client administrator to upload the company's approved seal/stamp and authorized signatory specimen, together with signatory name, designation and validity details.
•	Require explicit client authorization before a stored seal or signature asset may be applied to a system-generated PO, and allow immediate revocation or replacement.
•	Prevent users from viewing or accessing data belonging to another client organization.
FR-04 | Client Dashboard
The dashboard must show the client's current commercial and operational position.
•	Show total approved credit limit, current utilized exposure and indicative available credit.
•	Show outstanding amount, overdue amount and oldest overdue age based on the latest approved ledger data.
•	Show active POs, total PO quantity, dispatched quantity, pending PO quantity and recent dispatch requests.
•	Show payment updates awaiting client approval and Mundra Brothers verification.
•	Show pending balance confirmations and their due dates.
•	Show prominent warnings for low available credit, overdue payment terms, missing documents and dispatch blocks.
•	Provide quick actions for New PO, Request Dispatch, Report Payment, Request Ledger, Raise Issue and Upload Balance Confirmation.
FR-05 | Client Master and Commercial Terms
Mundra Brothers must configure the commercial controls applied to each client.
•	Maintain legal name, trade name, billing details, GST details, locations, contacts and status.
•	Set a standard credit limit for each client with effective dates and change history.
•	Set payment terms in days or another configured rule, including applicable grace periods.
•	Define which dispatch, invoice and ledger statuses count toward exposure. Undispatched PO balance must not consume credit unless Mundra Brothers later configures a separate reservation rule.
•	Define the client's approved products, delivery locations and any account-specific restrictions.
•	Support client suspension and reactivation with reason and approval.
FR-06 | Product and Rate Management
The system must calculate the correct applicable rate during PO entry.
•	Maintain product masters including grade, packaging, unit of measure and active status.
•	Maintain a generic/default rate for each product with effective-from and effective-to dates.
•	Allow client-specific product rates that override the generic rate for that client and period.
•	Show the applicable rate and rate source to authorized users during PO entry.
•	Prevent unauthorized manual rate editing by client users.
•	Require internal approval for rate creation, changes or exceptional one-time rates if configured.
•	Retain full rate history so older POs continue to display the rate applicable when they were placed.
•	When a new rate becomes effective, identify every older PO with an undelivered balance for the affected product/client scope and cancel that pending balance according to the approved rate-change rule.
•	Never alter the historical rate or quantity already dispatched under the old PO.
FR-07 | Purchase Order Creation and Initial Dispatch Choice
Authorized client users must be able to create a PO separately from the quantity they want dispatched immediately.
•	Capture client, project/site, delivery address, product, total PO quantity, unit, contact person, client PO reference and attachments.
•	Calculate total PO value using the applicable client-specific or generic rate and lock that rate on the submitted PO for audit history.
•	Require one of three initial dispatch choices: Full PO Quantity Immediately, Partial PO Quantity Immediately, or PO Only - No Dispatch Currently.
•	For Full PO Quantity Immediately, automatically create an initial dispatch request equal to the full PO quantity.
•	For Partial PO Quantity Immediately, require the immediate dispatch quantity and ensure it is greater than zero and not more than the total PO quantity.
•	For PO Only - No Dispatch Currently, create the PO without a dispatch request and without consuming credit for the undispatched quantity.
•	Require the client to choose one PO-document method: Upload Client-Generated PO or Generate Standard PO in Platform.
•	For Upload Client-Generated PO, require the signed/stamped PO file as an attachment before final submission, unless an authorized exception permits later upload.
•	For Generate Standard PO in Platform, populate the approved standard PO template from the entered PO, company, address, tax, product, quantity, rate and delivery information.
•	Allow draft saving before submission.
•	Route the PO and any initial dispatch instruction to the client's internal approver when maker-checker is enabled.
•	Display separate PO and dispatch acknowledgement numbers, quantities, submission times and statuses.
•	Allow PO amendment or cancellation only according to configurable status and dispatch-history rules.
FR-07C | PO Document, Seal, Signature and Timestamp
Every submitted PO must have a traceable authorized document, whether uploaded by the client or generated by the platform.
•	Support upload of PDF and approved image/document formats for a client-generated signed and stamped PO.
•	Extract or capture the client PO number, PO date and attachment version and link them permanently to the platform PO record.
•	Maintain one or more controlled standard PO templates with version number, effective dates and Mundra Brothers approval.
•	Generate a non-editable PDF from the standard template using the PO data recorded in the platform.
•	Where authorized, apply the client's stored company seal/stamp and authorized signatory image to the generated PDF.
•	Where a stronger digital-signature method is adopted, support an approved e-sign provider or digital certificate instead of relying only on an image of a signature.
•	Add a unique PO number, generation timestamp, submitting user, approving user, template version and verification reference or QR code to the generated document.
•	Apply the stored seal/signature only after all required client-side approvals are complete; a maker must not apply an approver's authority prematurely.
•	Prevent ordinary users from downloading or reusing raw seal/signature image files outside authorized document generation.
•	Any PO amendment after approval must create a new version or amendment document and preserve the original PDF and audit history.
FR-07A | Dispatch Release Management
A client must be able to request one or more dispatches against the open balance of an approved PO.
•	Show original PO quantity, cumulative dispatched quantity, quantities already requested, cancelled quantity and currently available balance.
•	Allow an authorized client user to create a dispatch request against the available PO balance, including quantity, requested date, site and delivery contact.
•	Prevent the total of completed and active dispatch requests from exceeding the open PO quantity.
•	Apply the PO's recorded rate only while that PO balance remains valid under the rate-change rule.
•	Run credit-limit, payment-term, balance-confirmation and compliance checks for each dispatch request at the time of release.
•	Allow multiple partial dispatches until the PO is fully dispatched, cancelled, expired or its pending balance is cancelled by a rate change.
FR-07B | Rate Change and Pending PO Balance Cancellation
A new applicable rate must prevent future dispatch under an older rate while preserving completed dispatch history.
•	When an authorized new generic or client-specific rate becomes effective, find all open older POs affected by that client, product and rate scope.
•	Cancel only the undelivered and unreleased balance under the old PO; quantities already dispatched or validly invoiced remain unchanged.
•	Cancel active but not yet finally approved dispatch requests under the old rate, unless an authorized exception explicitly preserves them.
•	Mark the PO as Partially Dispatched - Balance Cancelled Due to Rate Change or Cancelled Due to Rate Change, depending on dispatch history.
•	Notify the client that the old PO balance can no longer be dispatched and that a new PO must be raised at the currently applicable rate.
•	Record the old rate, new rate, effective time, cancelled quantity, affected POs and approving user in the audit trail.
FR-08 | Automated Dispatch Eligibility Engine
Every immediate or later dispatch request must be evaluated consistently before processing.
•	Check whether the client account and relevant product are active.
•	Check whether the proposed exposure after the requested dispatch quantity is within the approved credit limit.
•	Check whether any approved ledger amount is beyond the client's payment terms.
•	Check whether a mandatory quarterly balance confirmation is overdue beyond its configured cutoff date.
•	Check whether required client, PO or dispatch documents are available and valid.
•	Check whether a valid special approval covers the exact PO, dispatch, amount, quantity, date range or control violation.
•	For a PO Only submission, accept the PO after account, product, rate and document validation; defer credit and payment-term eligibility until dispatch is requested.
•	Auto-approve eligible dispatch requests or place them in a configurable Mundra review queue.
•	Block or hold ineligible dispatch requests and clearly state every reason, not only the first failed check.
FR-09 | Blocked Dispatch Resolution and Issue Raising
Clients must be able to challenge outdated or incorrect information without leaving the platform.
•	Display the failed rule, relevant amount/date and the action required to resolve it.
•	Allow the client to raise an issue directly from a blocked dispatch request.
•	Provide issue types such as Payment Already Made, Ledger Mismatch, Credit Limit Incorrect, Balance Confirmation Submitted, Rate Issue and Other.
•	Allow comments and supporting documents including payment proof and signed confirmations.
•	Route the issue to the correct Mundra Brothers queue with SLA and ownership.
•	Re-run dispatch eligibility automatically after the underlying approved data changes.
FR-10 | Payment Update Submission
Clients must be able to report payments with sufficient information for verification and downstream documentation.
•	Capture payment date, amount, payment mode, bank, UTR/reference number, payer account, remarks and proof attachment.
•	Allow the client to classify the payment as On Account or Against Specific Invoice(s).
•	For invoice allocation, allow one payment to be distributed across multiple invoices and validate that allocations plus permitted deductions equal the submitted amount.
•	Capture TDS and other permitted deductions separately, subject to final business rules.
•	Support client-side maker-checker approval before submission to Mundra Brothers.
•	Prevent duplicate payment submissions using reference number, amount, date and payer checks, while allowing authorized override with reason.
•	Show the client whether the payment is Submitted, Under Verification, Approved, Rejected or Requires Clarification.
FR-11 | Payment Verification and Ledger Effect
Mundra Brothers must verify payment information before it affects controlled financial data.
•	Route submitted payments to Mundra Brothers Accounts or another configured verification queue.
•	Allow verification, rejection, clarification request and corrected resubmission.
•	Keep client-reported payments visible as pending so blocked-dispatch messages can distinguish reported but unverified payments from no payment.
•	Only an approved payment may update the system's recognized payment position unless Mundra Brothers configures a provisional-credit rule.
•	Record verifier, date, comments and any changed allocation or TDS values.
•	Recalculate credit and dispatch eligibility immediately after payment approval or ledger refresh.
FR-12 | Refund Letter Generation
A refund letter must be generated from payment information in the approved Mundra Brothers format for submission to UltraTech.
•	Generate a draft refund letter as soon as a qualifying payment submission is created or approved, based on the configured workflow.
•	Populate client details, payment information, invoice allocations, on-account amount, TDS details and authorized signatory information from system data.
•	Use a controlled template with version history and effective dates.
•	Generate the output as PDF and an editable format if required.
•	Route the draft for Mundra Brothers review and approval before external dispatch when maker-checker is enabled.
•	Store generated versions, approval history, delivery status and any revised letter.
•	The exact refund purpose, recipient, calculation and UltraTech format remain subject to detailed confirmation.
FR-13 | Ledger Access and Requests
Clients must be able to obtain their ledger with minimal manual coordination.
•	Provide a one-click Request Ledger action for authorized client users.
•	If current ledger data is available and approved, generate or deliver it immediately.
•	If manual preparation is required, create a tracked service request for Mundra Brothers Accounts.
•	Allow selection of date range and file format, subject to available source data.
•	Show request status, delivered date and downloadable files in the client portal.
•	Maintain an audit trail of all ledger versions shared with the client.
FR-14 | Balance Confirmation Management
The product must automate the quarterly balance-confirmation lifecycle.
•	Create balance-confirmation periods, such as quarter ending 31 March, with configurable send and compliance due dates.
•	Retrieve the relevant client PDF from a configured Google Drive folder using a controlled client and period mapping.
•	Allow Mundra Brothers to send a confirmation manually or schedule automatic email delivery on a configured date.
•	Make the PDF available in the client's portal with instructions to sign, stamp and upload the completed document.
•	Allow the client to upload the signed/stamped confirmation and optionally add comments or report a mismatch.
•	Route the returned document to Mundra Brothers for approval, rejection or clarification.
•	Mark the period Complete only after an authorized Mundra Brothers user approves the returned document.
•	Block new dispatch requests after the configured cutoff when a mandatory confirmation remains incomplete. Example: a 31 March confirmation may block dispatches after 15 June if still pending.
•	Resume eligibility automatically after approval, subject to all other dispatch controls.
FR-15 | Special Approval and Exception Management
Mundra Brothers must be able to authorize controlled exceptions without weakening standard rules.
•	Allow authorized approvers to grant an exception for credit-limit breach, overdue payment terms, pending balance confirmation or another configured block.
•	Require reason, approving user, supporting note/document, start date, expiry date and scope.
•	Support scope by specific PO or dispatch request, maximum incremental amount, maximum total exposure, quantity, product or validity period.
•	Never treat a special approval as a permanent credit-limit or payment-term change unless explicitly converted through the master-data workflow.
•	Display the exception used on each approved dispatch and prevent use beyond its approved scope.
•	Notify relevant stakeholders when an exception is granted, used, nearing expiry or exhausted.
FR-16 | Mundra Brothers Administration Portal
Mundra Brothers must control the platform through role-based internal workspaces.
•	Provide separate queues for POs, dispatch requests, payments, issues, ledgers, refund letters and balance confirmations.
•	Allow creation of internal users with restricted access for accounts, PO/dispatch processing, approval and read-only needs.
•	Provide client master, rate, product, terms, credit and workflow configuration.
•	Show pending tasks by owner, age, priority and SLA.
•	Provide bulk but controlled actions where safe, such as sending balance confirmations or reminders.
•	Require elevated permission and full logging for credit, rate, exception and permission changes.
FR-17 | Notifications and Communication
The platform must proactively inform users about actions, risks and deadlines.
•	Support email and in-app notifications in the initial release.
•	Support browser or mobile push notifications if the application architecture permits and the user has consented.
•	Notify approvers immediately when an action requires approval.
•	Notify clients about payment due dates, overdue amounts, low available credit, blocked dispatches, clarification requests and pending balance confirmations.
•	Notify Mundra Brothers when clients submit POs or dispatch requests, report payments, raise issues or upload signed documents.
•	Allow configurable reminder cadence, templates, recipients and escalation levels.
•	Record delivery attempt, delivery result and user read status where supported.
FR-18 | Document Repository and Audit Trail
All transaction documents and decisions must remain traceable.
•	Store or securely reference purchase orders, payment proofs, ledgers, refund letters, balance confirmations and approval evidence.
•	Classify documents by client, transaction type, period, version and status.
•	Keep immutable audit records for login, creation, edits, submissions, approvals, rejections, downloads and configuration changes.
•	Show before-and-after values for material master-data changes.
•	Apply retention rules based on legal, accounting and business requirements.
7. Core Business Rules
7.1 PO and Dispatch Eligibility
A PO may be recorded without immediate dispatch, but a dispatch may proceed only when all mandatory checks pass or a valid authorized exception covers each failed check.
Rule	Pass Condition	Failure Outcome
Account status	Client and relevant users are active	Block PO or dispatch request
Rate	A valid generic or client-specific rate exists	Hold for rate review
Credit limit	Recognized exposure plus requested dispatch value does not exceed limit	Block dispatch or route for special approval
Payment terms	No recognized overdue amount breaches configured terms	Block or route for special approval
Balance confirmation	Required period is complete or cutoff has not passed	Block after cutoff
Required documents	All mandatory client/PO/dispatch documents are valid	Hold until resolved
PO authorization	Signed/stamped upload or approved system-generated PO is complete	Do not finalize PO
Client approval	Required client maker-checker approval is complete	Do not submit PO or dispatch externally

7.2 Indicative Exposure Formula
Working formula: Recognized Exposure = Approved Ledger Outstanding + Included Active Dispatch Value - Approved Unapplied Payments - Other Approved Adjustments. Available Credit = Approved Credit Limit + Active Exception Allowance - Recognized Exposure.

The exact inclusion of active dispatch requests, completed dispatches, invoices, provisional payments, TDS and debit/credit adjustments must be finalized during data-mapping workshops. Undispatched PO balance is excluded by default.
7.3 Rate Selection Priority
1.	Use an active client-specific product rate applicable on the PO date, if available.
2.	Otherwise use the active generic product rate applicable on the PO date.
3.	If neither exists, hold the PO for internal rate configuration; do not allow uncontrolled client-side rate entry.
7.4 Balance Confirmation Blocking Rule
Each confirmation period must have a document date, client response due date and dispatch-block date. The system must block new dispatch requests only when the configured dispatch-block date has passed and the status is not Complete. Mundra Brothers may grant a specific, time-bound exception. A PO may still be recorded without immediate dispatch if configured by Mundra Brothers.
7.5 Payment Recognition Rule
Client-submitted payments must be visible immediately as reported payments but must not silently change the approved ledger or recognized credit position. Recognition occurs only after configured Mundra Brothers verification, unless a documented provisional-credit policy is enabled.
7.6 PO and Dispatch Quantity Rule
PO quantity is the total commercial quantity authorized at a recorded rate. Dispatch quantity is the quantity requested for immediate or later supply. Credit and payment-term checks apply to the dispatch being released, not automatically to the full undispatched PO balance. Available PO Quantity = Original PO Quantity - Dispatched Quantity - Active Dispatch Quantity - Cancelled Quantity.
7.7 Rate Change Cancellation Rule
When a new applicable rate becomes effective, any undelivered balance under an affected older-rate PO becomes ineligible for future dispatch and is cancelled. The client must raise a new PO at the new rate. Completed dispatches and invoices retain their original PO rate and history.
7.8 PO Authorization Rule
A PO is considered authorized only when the client uploads its own valid signed/stamped PO or the platform generates the approved standard PO after the required maker-checker approvals. Stored seal and signature assets may be applied only under explicit client authorization and must remain protected from ordinary download or reuse.
8. End-to-End Workflows
8.1 Client PO and Initial Dispatch Workflow
1.	Client PO Maker enters the total PO quantity, product, site, applicable rate data and other required details.
2.	The client selects Full Immediate Dispatch, Partial Immediate Dispatch or PO Only - No Dispatch Currently.
3.	The client uploads its own signed/stamped PO or selects platform generation using the approved standard template.
4.	If client maker-checker is enabled, the PO and dispatch instruction go to the Client PO Approver.
5.	After approval, the system stores or generates the final authorized PO PDF with timestamp and audit reference.
6.	For PO Only, the PO is accepted without dispatch credit consumption after basic account, product, rate and document validation.
7.	For full or partial dispatch, the system calculates the requested dispatch value and proposed exposure.
8.	The eligibility engine checks credit, overdue terms, balance confirmation, account status and documents for that dispatch quantity.
9.	If all checks pass, the dispatch becomes Auto-Approved or Pending Mundra Processing according to configuration.
10.	If any check fails, the dispatch becomes Blocked or Exception Review and the client sees all reasons.
11.	The client may report a payment, upload a document or raise an issue from the blocked dispatch.
12.	Mundra Brothers may resolve the underlying data or issue a scoped special approval.
13.	The system re-runs checks and releases the dispatch only when every failure is resolved or covered.
8.2 Later Partial Dispatch Workflow
1.	The client opens an active PO and reviews original, dispatched, active, cancelled and available quantities.
2.	The client enters a new dispatch quantity against the open PO balance.
3.	The platform validates that the quantity does not exceed the available PO quantity and that the PO rate remains valid.
4.	The dispatch request follows client approval if configured and then the full dispatch eligibility checks.
5.	Approved dispatch quantity is reserved and, after completion, added to cumulative dispatched quantity.
6.	The PO closes when fully dispatched or when its remaining balance is cancelled or expired.
8.3 Rate Change and Old PO Closure Workflow
1.	An authorized Mundra Brothers user approves a new rate with an effective date and scope.
2.	The system finds affected older-rate POs with an undelivered balance.
3.	The system preserves dispatched/invoiced history and cancels the remaining old-rate balance and ineligible pending dispatch requests.
4.	The client and relevant Mundra Brothers users receive the cancellation quantity, old rate, new rate and effective date.
5.	The client raises a new PO for future dispatch at the newly applicable rate.
8.4 Payment and Refund-Letter Workflow
1.	Client Payment Maker enters payment details, chooses On Account or invoice-wise allocation, records TDS and uploads proof.
2.	If client approval is enabled, a Client Payment Approver verifies and submits it.
3.	The system performs duplicate and allocation validations.
4.	Mundra Brothers Accounts verifies the payment and may approve, reject or request clarification.
5.	The system creates the refund letter at the configured stage using the approved template and transaction data.
6.	If internal maker-checker applies, the refund letter is reviewed and approved before sending to UltraTech.
7.	The final letter and delivery record are stored against the payment.
8.	Approved payment data triggers exposure recalculation and re-evaluation of relevant blocked dispatch requests.
8.5 Balance Confirmation Workflow
1.	Mundra Brothers creates or imports the confirmation period and maps the client PDF in Google Drive.
2.	The platform sends the PDF manually or automatically on the scheduled date.
3.	The client downloads, signs and stamps the document, then uploads the completed PDF.
4.	Mundra Brothers reviews the returned document.
5.	If correct, the confirmation is approved and marked Complete; otherwise clarification is requested.
6.	Reminder notifications continue until completion.
7.	If the configured block date passes while incomplete, new dispatch requests are blocked automatically.
8.	Approval of the document removes this block and triggers dispatch re-evaluation.
