14. Non-Functional Requirements
Area	Requirement
Security	Encryption in transit and at rest; strong password storage; least-privilege access; secure session cookies; protection against common web vulnerabilities
Tenant isolation	No client organization may access another client's users, POs, dispatches, payments, ledger or documents
Availability	Target availability and maintenance window to be agreed; critical PO, dispatch and approval functions require monitored service
Performance	Typical dashboard and list views should load within 3 seconds under expected operating volume; eligibility decisions should return promptly
Auditability	Material actions must be attributable to a named user and timestamp, with before-and-after values where applicable
Data integrity	Idempotent submissions, duplicate detection, controlled status transitions and transactional updates for financial records
Usability	Responsive web experience for desktop and mobile; clear business language; accessible forms and actionable error messages
Privacy	Collect only required personal information; provide retention, deletion and access controls consistent with applicable law and contracts
Backup and recovery	Automated backups, tested restoration process and agreed recovery point/recovery time targets
Observability	Monitoring for failed integrations, notification failures, document-generation errors and unusual authentication activity
Configurability	Credit rules, dates, reminders, templates, approval routes and permissions should be configurable without code changes where practical

15. Acceptance Criteria
•	A client user can log in, remain securely signed in for the configured period and access only their organization's information.
•	A Client Organization Admin can create users and restrict one user to PO/dispatch entry while another user can only approve payments.
•	The system selects a client-specific rate over a generic rate and preserves the applied rate on the PO.
•	A client can create a 500-tonne PO and choose full immediate dispatch, a smaller partial dispatch or PO Only with no immediate dispatch.
•	For a 500-tonne PO with a 200-tonne immediate dispatch, credit and payment-term eligibility is calculated on the 200-tonne dispatch value, not the full PO value.
•	A PO Only submission records the commercial PO without consuming credit for the undispatched quantity.
•	A client can request later partial dispatches against the available PO balance without exceeding the original quantity.
•	When a new applicable rate becomes effective, the system preserves completed old-rate dispatches but cancels the undelivered old-rate PO balance and requires a new PO.
•	A client can upload its own signed/stamped PO or generate the standard PO inside the platform.
•	A platform-generated PO is produced only after required approval and includes the approved seal/signature treatment, timestamp, template version and verification reference.
•	A dispatch within credit and payment terms, with compliant balance confirmation, follows the configured approval path without manual rule checking.
•	A dispatch exceeding credit or payment terms is blocked or routed for exception approval with all reasons visible to the client.
•	A client can report a payment against one or more invoices or on account, including proof and TDS information.
•	A pending payment is visible but does not incorrectly alter approved exposure before verification.
•	An approved payment triggers a refund-letter draft from the correct template and recalculates relevant dispatch eligibility.
•	A client can request a ledger in one action and track delivery status.
•	The system retrieves the correct client-period balance-confirmation PDF from Google Drive and prevents cross-client document leakage.
•	A signed/stamped balance confirmation can be uploaded, reviewed and marked complete only by an authorized Mundra Brothers user.
•	Dispatch requests are blocked after the configured balance-confirmation cutoff and automatically reconsidered after completion or a valid exception.
•	A special approval cannot be used outside its amount, PO/dispatch, product or time scope.
•	All approvals, rejections, credit changes, rate changes and permission changes appear in the audit trail.
•	Email and in-app notifications are generated for configured approval, payment, credit and compliance triggers.
