17. Assumptions, Dependencies and Open Questions
17.1 Confirmed Working Assumptions
•	The product will be a secure white-label web application under Mundra Brothers branding.
•	UltraTech invoices clients directly; this software manages the Mundra Brothers control and coordination layer.
•	Both client organizations and Mundra Brothers require multiple users with role-based restrictions and approvals.
•	Credit limit, payment terms, generic rates and client-specific rates will be maintained by authorized Mundra Brothers users.
•	A PO and a dispatch request are separate records: one PO may support multiple dispatch releases.
•	Undispatched PO quantity does not consume credit by default; eligibility is checked when dispatch is requested.
•	A new applicable rate cancels any undelivered balance under an affected older-rate PO, requiring a new PO for future dispatch.
•	Clients may either upload their own signed/stamped PO or authorize generation through the platform's standard PO template.
•	Balance confirmations are required periodically and may become a mandatory condition for future dispatches after a configured cutoff.
•	Google Drive is the initial source for balance-confirmation PDFs.
17.2 Details Required Before Final PRD Sign-Off
Topic	Clarification Needed
Refund letter	Exact business purpose, recipient, approved sample format, mandatory fields, trigger stage, signatory and how UltraTech responds.
TDS	Applicable calculation rules, certificate requirements, invoice allocation behaviour, rounding and treatment in available credit.
Ledger source	Whether ledger is uploaded manually, synchronized from UltraTech, generated from Tally or built from platform transactions.
Credit exposure	Which PO/dispatch/invoice statuses count toward exposure and whether pending/provisional payments reduce it.
Payment terms	Whether overdue is calculated invoice-wise, ledger-wise or through a value/age threshold; applicable grace periods.
Dispatch fulfillment	Steps after approval, including UltraTech order placement, acknowledgement, allocation, dispatch, invoice and completion data.
